ut","url":"https://www.meetup.com/west-end-womens-social-circle/events/316713265/","description":"This Is A Ladies Event Only And If You RSVP And Are Unable To Attend Please Change Your RSVP As A Courtesy!!\n\nWhen arriving ask the hostess for the west end women's social.\n\nJoin us for a fun-filled evening at our West End Women's Hangout! This event is perfect for professional women, girlfriends, and ladies looking to hang out and make long lasting friendships.\n\nConnect with like-minded women in a relaxed and welcoming atmosphere where you can unwind and enjoy some quality girl time. Whether you're new to the area or a long-time resident, our social circle is all about building connections and creating lasting friendships.\n\nCome ready to socialize, laugh, and make memories with a fantastic group of women. Don't miss out on this opportunity to have a blast with the West End Women's Social Circle!","startDate":"2026-10-09T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Kelseys Original Roadhouse","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"3970 Grand Park Dr, Mississauga, ON L5B 4M6, Canada, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"West End Women's Social","url":"https://www.meetup.com/west-end-womens-social-circle/"},"performer":"West End Women's Social"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Mississauga- let’s speak French/ Parlons français","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/events/314154988/","description":"Let’s get together to speak French! We’ll enjoy tea/coffee and some icebreaker games. Everyone is welcome.\n\nVenez parler français!\n\nÀ bientôt,\n\nHassane.\n\n\\*Merci beaucoup de vous être inscrit(e) à notre prochaine rencontre! Nous sommes ravis de votre présence.\nAfin de permettre à d’autres de se joindre à nous, nous vous demandons respectueusement :\n\n1. **Si vos plans changent,** veuillez mettre à jour votre statut (passer à 'Non') le plus rapidement possible pour libérer votre place.\n2. **Si vous êtes sur la liste d'attente,** merci de ne pas vous présenter à l'événement. Votre statut doit être confirmé pour pouvoir participer. Veuillez vous inscrire directement aux prochaines dates disponibles.\n\nAu plaisir de vous accueillir!\n\n\\*To allow others to join us, we respectfully ask that you:\n\n* **If your plans change,** please update your RSVP status (change it to 'No') as quickly as possible to free up your spot.\n* **If you are on the waiting list,** please do not show up for the event. Your status must be confirmed to participate. Instead, please register directly for the next available dates.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nVeuillez noter que pour profiter pleinement de nos échanges, une aptitude de base à la conversation est vivement souhaitée : ce groupe est un cercle de discussion convivial et non un cours de langue.\n\nPlease note that to fully enjoy the experience, a basic speaking aptitude is recommended: this group is a social conversation circle, not a formal teaching class.\n\nWe look forward to welcoming you!\n\nPlease join our WhatsApp group:\n\nhttps://chat.whatsapp.com/LRUdXbjpG8I9aph4dU6Go8","startDate":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Chocolate and love cafe","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"5985 Rodeo Dr Unit 14, Mississauga, ON L5R 3V6,, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/"},"performer":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Kojève and Law: A Critical Examination","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-toronto-philosophy-meetup/events/316262447/","description":"Alexandre Kojève (1902–1968) was one of the major philosophers of the twentieth century. His famous lectures on Hegel and his provocative end-of-history thesis left an indelible mark on contemporary thought. By the end of the Second World War, he abandoned academic philosophy to embark on a diplomatic career. While occupying an influential position in French foreign trade diplomacy, Kojève worked on a series of manuscripts which largely remained unpublished until well after his death. Initially dismissed as post-historical irony and play, Kojève’s post-war philosophical writings open new perspectives on how we became post-historical and where we go from here.\n\nSpotlighting Kojeve's distinct contributions to legal scholarship, while also showcasing his broader influence across a range of disciplines — including philosophy, political theory, sociology, law and transnational studies — these two books include original contributions from eminent editors, translators, and biographers of Kojeve, as well as from historians of legal and political thought, specialists on global trade and private international law, statelessness, and public international law.\n\nFirst Panel - Kojève and the Ancients.\n\n* Participants: Jonas Schwab-Plfug, Luis Pedrazuela, and Teresa Pullano\n* Discussant: David Ragazzoni\n\nSecond Panel - Kojève and His Contemporaries.\n\n* Participants: Matthew Sharpe, Massimo Palma, and Igor Shoikhedbrod\n* Discussant: Clifford Orwin\n\nThird panel - Kojève and the Moderns. Between Kant and Hegel.\n\n* Participants: Bryan-Paul Frost and Jacob McNulty\n* Discussants: Alan Brudner and Susan Shell\n\nFourth panel - Kojève and Phenomenology.\n\n* Participants: William Conklin, Bogdan Ovcharuk, and Sabina Tortorella\n* Discussant: Tarek Dika.\n\nFifth panel - Kojève, Empire, and the Future of the Universal Homogeneous State.\n\n* Participants: Rob Howse and Olga Obolenets.\n* Discussants: Ronald Beiner and Melissa Williams\n\n**\\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\***\n\nThis is a book launch on [Kojeve and Law: A Critical Examination](https://www.routledge.com/Kojeve-and-Law-A-Critical-Examination/Shoikhedbrod/p/book/9781032734118) (Routledge 2026) presented by the University of Toronto's Centre for Ethics. The conference is free to attend and open to the public. Talks will be streamed online with live chat.\n\nAbout the Centre for Ethics (http://ethics.utoronto.ca):\n\nThe Centre for Ethics is an interdisciplinary centre aimed at advancing research and teaching in the field of ethics, broadly defined. The Centre seeks to bring together the theoretical and practical knowledge of diverse scholars, students, public servants and social leaders in order to increase understanding of the ethical dimensions of individual, social, and political life.\n\nIn pursuit of its interdisciplinary mission, the Centre fosters lines of inquiry such as (1) foundations of ethics, which encompasses the history of ethics and core concepts in the philosophical study of ethics; (2) ethics in action, which relates theory to practice in key domains of social life, including bioethics, business ethics, and ethics in the public sphere; and (3) ethics in translation, which draws upon the rich multiculturalism of the City of Toronto and addresses the ethics of multicultural societies, ethical discourse across religious and cultural boundaries, and the ethics of international society.\n\nThe Ethics of A.I. Lab at the Centre For Ethics recently appeared on a list of 10 organizations leading the way in ethical A.I.: https://ocean.sagepub.com/blog/10-organizations-leading-the-way-in-ethical-ai","startDate":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Larkin Building, Room 200","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"15 Devonshire Place, University of Toronto, Toronto, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"The Toronto Philosophy Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-toronto-philosophy-meetup/"},"performer":"The Toronto Philosophy Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"AWS YouthTech x SBG Sheridan Bootcamp","url":"https://www.meetup.com/aws-sbg-at-sheridan-college-davis-campus/events/316769723/","description":"**[Register now : AWS YouthTech X SBG Sheridan Bootcamp](https://luma.com/p3yhr7xo)**\n​Get ready for a high-energy afternoon at the AWS YouthTech × SBG Sheridan Bootcamp! Hosted by the AWS Student Builder Group at Sheridan College, this afternoon event is packed with learning, fresh ideas, and plenty of chances to explore what you can build with cloud and AI/ML technology. Whether you want to pick up practical skills, hear from people working with AWS, or spend a few hours in a room buzzing with momentum, there will be something worth showing up for.\n​Spots are limited-register early to secure yours!\n\n## ​**What to expect**\n\n* ​**Expert Sessions:** Hear directly from industry leaders and experienced AWS practitioners through cloud fundamentals talks, an AI/ML presentation, and an employee panel.\n* ​**Hands-on Workshop:** Roll up your sleeves and build real-world cloud and AI/ML skills in an interactive technical workshop.\n* ​**Kahoot & Prizes:** Join the fun and compete for a chance to win a coffee chat with a recruiter.\n* ​**Networking:** Connect with peers and professionals across the GTA who share your interest in cloud and tech.\n* ​**Resume drop at closing:** At the end of the event, attendees can submit their resume to a dedicated pool shared with recruiters.\n\n​*Come ready to learn, meet people, and make the most of an afternoon built for students who want a closer look at AWS and where it can take them.*\n\n## ​**Event Details**\n\n​**When:** Friday, October 9, 2026\n**Time:** 1:00 PM - 5:00 PM\n**Where: Room A145,** Sheridan HMC (Hazel McCallion Campus), Mississauga\n**Cost:** Free\n\nNOTE : [Luma](https://luma.com/p3yhr7xo) registration is required to confirm your spot. ONLY FOR ACTIVE STUDENTS FORM COLLEGES/UNIVERSITY ACROSS GTA","startDate":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Sheridan College - Hazel McCallion Campus","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"4180 Duke of York Blvd, Mississauga, ON L5B 0H7, Canada, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"AWS SBG at Sheridan College - Davis Campus","url":"https://www.meetup.com/aws-sbg-at-sheridan-college-davis-campus/"},"performer":"AWS SBG at Sheridan College - Davis Campus"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto Downtown Semi-formal Singles Mixer (Age 35 and under)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/do-stuff-and-make-friends-in-toronto/events/316344775/","description":"NOTE: This is a paid event.\n\nTickets here: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/toronto-downtown-semi-formal-singles-mixer-age-35-and-under-tickets-1999224525373?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true\n\nJoin us at the beautiful Spirit of York downtown Toronto for our semi-formal singles mixer. Dress to impress.\n\nCalling all Toronto singles! Join us for our biggest and best singles mixer. We got over 200 people out last time, so let's make this one even bigger!\n\nJoin us at the beautiful Spirit of York Distillery and meet a room full of singles at your leisure. Then pull up their profile on your phone, and give them a Like or a Pass. They will do the same for you, and matches are sent the following day.\n\nThe dress code is semi-formal for this event, so dress to impress! This one is for singlse aged 35 and under.\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Please create a profile on www.15FirstDates.ca using the same email you used on Eventbrite. You will need a profile if you'd like to participate in the in-person swiping. You do not need a profile to attend our event.\n\nThe mix and mingle will be from 8-10:30pm, followed by a DJ dance party.\n\nWe got over 200 guests last time downtown Toronto, so don't miss out!","startDate":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Spirit of York Distillery Co.","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"PE","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"12 Trinity Street, Toronto, PE"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Do Stuff and Make Friends in Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/do-stuff-and-make-friends-in-toronto/"},"performer":"Do Stuff and Make Friends in Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🎬Movie: Other Mommy  -  Food & Drinks after the movie 🍿!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316155472/","description":"🎬 Let’s Go to the Movies (and Actually Talk… or Not)\n\nWhether you're a film nerd, popcorn enthusiast, or just looking for a chill night out with interesting people — this one's for you.\n\nWe’re heading out to see a movie together, then grabbing food or drinks after. If the film's great (or terrible), we’ll probably talk about it forever. If it’s just okay, we’ll talk about it for 10 minutes and move on to everything else — books, dating apps, weird dreams, how Toronto keeps getting more expensive, etc.\n\nThe vibe is relaxed, friendly, and not too serious. No film degree needed. No icebreakers. No pressure to “perform.” Just come enjoy the film, connect with some thoughtful people, and see where the night goes Click here to watch trailer!\n\n🎞️ **Movie Title + Trailer:**[ \\[Click here to watch trailer!\\]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pPxrX9ukWBY)\n\n📖 **📖 Plot Summary:** A terrifying, supernatural trip into the darkening world of a young girl as her family, and their home, are haunted by a sinister entity that is determined to take up residence inside her. But first, it needs to persuade her to let it in …\n\n***\n\n### 🗓️ **Event Details**\n\n📍 **Meetup Time:** 6:00 PM (Final time + theatre announced Tuesday of event week)\n🎬 **Movie Start Time:** TBA\n⏱️ **Runtime:** TBA\n📌 **Meetup Spot:** To be confirmed (based on theatre)\n🎟️ **Cost:**\n\n* **$11.50** for *CineClub* members\n* **$16.00** regular admission\n👉 You are responsible for buying your own ticket.\n\n**🪑 Reserved Seating:**\nYou must buy your ticket *before* signing up. You'll be asked where you're sitting so we can all sit together! However, members are welcome to sit anywhere that works for them.\n🎫 Buy your ticket here: [https://www.cineplex.com](https://www.cineplex.com)\n📍🪑 **Where I will be sitting:**\n\n🍿 **After the Movie:**\nYes, we’re heading out after! It’s not just a movie night — it’s a social night. Let's talk, laugh, and dissect every plot twist.\n\n***\n\n### ✅ **Before You Sign Up**\n\n* Please **buy your ticket first** — seating is limited!\n* When signing up, let us know your **seat number** so we can try to group everyone together.\n* You can still sign up or just **show up on the day** if you’re not sure you can make it — we’re flexible!\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here to join](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)\n🎟️ **Join Cineplex’s CineClub for discounts**: [https://www.cineplex.com/cineclub](https://www.cineplex.com/cineclub)\n🎁 **Get your SCENE Card** for free movies and points: [https://www.scene.ca](https://www.scene.ca)\n\n***\n\n### 🎥 **A Quick Word About Movie Etiquette**\n\nWe love a great film experience. Please:\n\n* Turn off your phone\n* Don’t talk during the movie\n* Be respectful of others\n\nRepeat offenders will be removed from the group — we take our cinema seriously (but with snacks).\n\n***\n\n### 👥 **About the Group**\n\nThis event is open to everyone — single, not single, shy, social, new in town or a long-time local. We're a group for people who love movies *and* making real connections. We also do walks, hikes, restaurants, arts & culture — come be part of it!\n🎬 **Organized by:** Mathew\n📧 Questions? Reach out: **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**","startDate":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Casual Board Games and Pub Social After","url":"https://www.meetup.com/boardgamestoronto/events/316441924/","description":"The Board Games event is a fun, sociable and charitable event\n\nWe are a fun, friendly and kind group of people mostly in our 20s, 30s and 40s. Beginners are welcome! We are a very inclusive and social group and we teach people how to play games they have not played before :)\n\nWe provide a variety of 40+ board games. The games usually take 5 or 10 minutes to learn and 30 to 60 minutes to play.\n\nPlay in French: On the last Friday of the month, we're offering a table where the games are played in French. Anyone with an intermediate level of French who wants to practice while playing is welcome to join. Just ask for Philippe when you arrive.\n\n**Time**\n\n*Board Games Start time: 630pm\n- Board Games end time: 10pm\n*Eat / Drink/ Socialise at a nearby pub afterwards\n\n**Location**\n\n30 Leeds St, Toronto, ON M6G 3R8 (Ukrainian Catholic Church of the Holy Protection)\n\nThe entrance to the board game room is at the back of the Church. There is a sign on the door that says BOARD GAMES GROUP.\n\nPlease use the map provided on the event page also.\n\nPayment\n**There are two ways to pay**\n**10 by Cash - coins are not accepted. Only bills.****\n**11.55 by Debit/Credit card\n\n**Charity Donations**\n\n- This is a not-for-profit initiative. Revenue go towards covering costs of the event including venue, insurance marketing, refreshments and board games. Any surplus revenue is donated to charity\n\n**Food and drink**\n\n*Everyone will get cookies/candy for free\n- Cups will be provided for tap water\n*Bring your own food and drink.\n- Please do not bring CHIPS AND CRACKERS as they make a mess and are greasy\n***ALCOHOL IS PROHIBITED AND WE HAVE A ZERO TOLERANCE POLICY ON THIS - there are no second chances**\n\nPhotos will be taken at the event and posted publicly for marketing purposes. Please only attend if you are ok with this or tell me when you arrive that you do not want to be in any photos\n\nThe event is officially hosted by Ace of Math Learning Program Ontario Inc.","startDate":"2026-10-09T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Ukrainian Catholic Church of the Holy Protection","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"30 Leeds St, Toronto, ON M6G 3R8, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Board Games and Social","url":"https://www.meetup.com/boardgamestoronto/"},"performer":"Board Games and Social"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"TOPHATs Asian Comedy $$ and Waterworks Happy Hour","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/events/316747942/","description":"Join Lawrence, your top hatted host, for an evening of Crafty goodness, Local food and Asian Comedy.\n\nAt 5:30pmish we will meet-up at the Waterwork Bar. I'll be there a little early to secure a table for our group, so look for my top hat.\n\nhttps://www.waterworksfoodhall.com/restaurants/waterworks-bar\n\nThere are lots of food options in the Waterwork Food Hall.\nMy eye is on Hanoi Bites Vietnamese sandwich, though Rasta Pasta may be my meal if I am more hungry.\n\nhttps://www.waterworksfoodhall.com/restaurants\n\nAt 7pmish we will walk over to The Rivoli, where we’re escaping Thanksgiving with an all-Asian comedy lineup featuring headliner Rahul Topiwala, birthday boy and host Anto Man-Ming Chan, Alia Rasul, Rush Kazi and Jordan Hanoun.\n\nBig laughs, great comedians, and absolutely no obligation to sit through your racist uncle’s dinner-table material.\n\nFollow the link below for your tickets on Eventbrite $22.90 or you can pay more at the Door.\n\n[asiancomedyallstars.eventbrite.com](https://asiancomedyallstars.eventbrite.com/?fbclid=IwZXh0bgNhZW0CMTAAcGRvZgVicmlkETEwNGpuU2h6OUtrNFZucnRQc3J0YwZhcHBfaWQQMjIyMDM5MTc4ODIwMDg5MgABHvY-guwsm5bXVN7IJxWFHjc9CBZ4MARk97Xg8cCPf_X1q-u6czMfJceDrJ45_aem_9fpi8sYDZUWdwW_o4NpQLg)","startDate":"2026-10-09T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Waterworks Food Hall","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"50 Brant St, Toronto, ON M5V 3G9, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Beer Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/"},"performer":"Toronto Beer Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Tantric Family Constellation: Temple of Love & Money","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316629915/","description":"**TANTRIC FAMILY CONSTELLATIONS**\n**Tantric Temple Mysteries**\n\n**This is the project overview only.**\n**Themes and dates may change.**\n\n**To find the exact topic, date and register, please join:**\n\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**About this event**\n\n**Tantric Family Constellations is a group practice combining Archetypal / Family Constellations with a living tantric Temple space.**\n\n**Each meeting has its own theme.**\n\n**For example:**\n\n**Love & Money • Ancient Languages of Love • Love & Loneliness • Masculine & Feminine • Desire & Freedom • Relationship Patterns**\n\n**The theme gives us a field to explore — but every participant discovers their own personal story inside it.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Part 1 — Discover your pattern**\n\n**We begin by exploring different dimensions of the evening’s theme together.**\n\n**Then each participant goes through a mini-constellation to see their own pattern, model or hidden dynamic.**\n\n**Instead of only thinking about the question, you can see how its different forces are arranged for you:**\n\n**What attracts you?**\n**What do you avoid?**\n**Where does your energy stop?**\n**What are you moving toward?**\n\n**This creates a personal map for the second part of the evening.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Part 2 — Enter the Temple**\n\n**Then we open the Tantric Temple.**\n\n**The constellation points become living centers in the space.**\n\n**Participants are free to move between them, following their own inner process.**\n\n**You may stay with one energy, move toward another, step away, return, observe what happens in your body, or allow yourself to gradually absorb a quality that previously felt distant.**\n\n**At the same time, you encounter other participants moving through their own paths.**\n\n**Through presence, movement and consensual interaction, the personal constellation becomes a living group field.**\n\n**There is no fixed choreography and no need to perform.**\n\n**You follow your own rhythm.**\n\n**The practice is about allowing yourself to experience, embody and integrate the different energies of the constellation rather than only understand them intellectually.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Why “Temple”?**\n\n**The Temple is a temporary tantric space where symbolic and archetypal energies can be experienced through the body, movement and connection with others.**\n\n**The journey is individual, but it happens inside a shared field.**\n\n**You may discover that a quality which looked abstract during the constellation becomes much more understandable once you can actually move toward it, stay with it and experience it in contact with others.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**No previous constellation or tantra experience is required.**\n\n**Participation is voluntary, and you can always choose your own level of involvement and contact.**\n\n**The space is based on:**\n\n**consent • respect • confidentiality • personal boundaries • freedom of movement**\n\n**This is a transpersonal personal-growth practice, not a sexual event.**\n\n**Details, themes, dates and registration:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n\n**Вот более естественный и аккуратный английский вариант, сохраняя твой простой стиль:**\n\n**TICKETS**\n\n1. **Regular Ticket — $100 CAD**\n1. **Early Bird Ticket — $65 CAD**\n**If you register and pay before August 31.**\n**3. Supportive Ticket — $55 CAD**\n**For people with limited financial resources.**\n**4. Bring a Friend — $150 CAD for 2 people**\n\n**If the price is too much for you, send a personal message on Telegram: t.me/AndyTherapist to ask about volunteer options.**\n\n**HOW TO PAY**\n\n**Send an Interac e-Transfer to:**\n**andy.litvinov@gmail.com**\n**After payment, send a screenshot of the confirmation to: t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**Please mention which event you are registering for.**\n\n**After registration, you will be added to the participants’ group.**\n\n**If you have any questions, feel free to message:**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**Toronto Tantra community:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**","startDate":"2026-10-09T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Cuddle Club - platonic body nourishing.","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316629411/","description":"**CUDDLE CLUB.**\n**Have you tried that?**\n\n**In Amsterdam cuddle events are sold out quickly. Even few different Cuddle clubs are happening at the same day. It's so popular there.**\n\n**In Toronto there** **is** **nearly no Cuddle clubs yet.**\n**But we are doing that.**\n**Join our tantric group and leave a message in comments if you wanna join the waiting list.**\n**T.me/TorontoTantra**\n**___**\n**About this event**\n**• What is the cuddle club?**\n\n**It’s a cozy evening to experience how deeply nourishing it can feel to be held, without any romantic or sexual expectations. A space where people can come together to share love and touch. We cuddle platonically, the way you’d hold a child or a kitten.**\n\n**• What will we be doing?**\n\n**Facilitator will guide you through some gentle exercises to help you unwind after your day, soften into your body, and calm your nervous system. We aim to make you feel safe in your own body, which can help you connect with others.**\n\n**• Cuddle puddle perfection**\n\n**Everything is by invitation, but we will guide you into a beautifully structured cuddle puddle. It is a very comfortable, welcoming way of cuddling where you are held and touched by multiple people at the same time. Chances are you’ll float home afterwards, high on oxytocin.**\n\n**• Important terms & agreements:**\n1. **Keep it platonic: we cuddle without romantic or sexual expectations or escalations**\n1. **Take care of yourself and others: communicate and respect boundaries**\n1. **Be here fully: This is a sober space. No drugs, no alcohol. No phones.**\n\n**Details in telegram group:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n\n**TICKETS**\n**Regular Ticket — $50 CAD**\n**Early Bird Ticket — $35 CAD (If you register and pay before August 31).**\n**Supportive Ticket — $25 CAD (For students and people with low financial income).**\n**Combo — $60 CAD for 2 people (Bring a friend).**\n\n**Free participation.**\n**We want everyone to have an opportunity to participate. If the price is too much for you, send a personal message on Telegram: t.me/AndyTherapist to ask about volunteer options.**\n\n**If you have any questions, feel free to message:**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**","startDate":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"MASSAGE CLUB & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316628956/","description":"MASSAGE CLUB & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY\nThis is the project overview only!\nDates might change.\n\nTo find the exact dates and register for the event, please join our Telegram group:\n\nT.me/TorontoTantra\nT.me/AndyTherapist\n\nMASSAGE & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY CLUB\n\nHave you ever explored massage not only as relaxation, but also as a way to reconnect with your body, emotions, and nervous system?\n\nIn Toronto there are many massage services, but not many spaces where people can safely learn, practice and exchange conscious touch together.\n\nWe would like to create such a club.\n\nA warm, respectful space for people interested in massage, bodywork, somatic practices and body-oriented psychotherapy.\n\nYou don’t need professional massage experience. Beginners are welcome.\n\nJoin our group and leave a message if you would like to be added to the waiting list.\nt.me/TorontoTantra\n\nAbout this event\n\n• What is the Massage & Body Psychotherapy Club?\n\nIt is a practice evening where we explore conscious touch, relaxation, massage techniques and simple body-oriented therapeutic exercises.\n\nThe purpose is not only to relax muscles, but also to develop better contact with your body, reduce stress and learn how safe touch can support emotional regulation and connection.\n\n• What will we be doing?\n\nDepending on the evening, we may explore:\n\n- simple relaxation massage techniques\n- conscious touch and body awareness\n- grounding and nervous-system regulation\n- breathing and relaxation exercises\n- somatic and body-psychotherapy exercises\n- practicing giving and receiving\n- communication of boundaries and consent\n\nPractices can be done in pairs or small groups and will be guided step by step.\n\n• Massage exchange\n\nOne of the main parts of the club is a structured massage exchange.\n\nYou can experience both sides:\ngiving touch and receiving touch.\n\nThe goal is not to perform a “perfect massage,” but to become more sensitive to another person’s body, learn to listen through your hands, communicate clearly and discover what kind of touch feels supportive.\n\nImportant terms & agreements\n\nConsent first: every exercise and every touch is optional.\n\nRespect boundaries: you can say yes, no, stop, slower, softer or change the practice at any moment.\n\nKeep it therapeutic: this is a bodywork and personal-development space, not a sexual service or dating event.\n\nStay present: no alcohol or recreational drugs during the event.\n\nConfidentiality: personal experiences shared during the practice stay within the group.\n\nThe club may be interesting for people curious about:\n\nmassage • bodywork • somatic therapy • body-oriented psychotherapy • conscious touch • nervous-system regulation • relaxation • tantra-inspired body awareness\n\nDetails, dates and registration:\nt.me/TorontoTantra","startDate":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Friday VIP Future Nightclub for free for ladies ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/nightlife-society-vip-club-nights/events/316654615/","description":"🎉 Future Nightclub Fridays \\| VIP Night Out 🎉\n📍 Future Nightclub\n🗓 Every Friday\n⏰ 10:30 PM\nJoin us this Friday for a fun VIP night out at Future Nightclub.\n✅ Free entry until 11:30 pm\n\nJust say “Ammar Alomari” at the door for the guestlist.\nFor the guys check on the guest list to get your free drink and a discount for the door cover.\n\n🥂 VIP booth access and free entry before 12 midnight\n\nComing alone? No worries. We usually have 40+ people joining every weekend, including friends, ticket guests, and new people from our meetup group, so you will have people to connect with.\n📌 Find us at the main booth.\n\n🙌 19+ only with valid government-issued ID. Entry is subject to venue rules, capacity, and door policy.\nSee you Friday!","startDate":"2026-10-10T02:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Future","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"570 Queen St W, Toronto, ON M5V 2B5, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Nightlife Society | VIP Club Nights","url":"https://www.meetup.com/nightlife-society-vip-club-nights/"},"performer":"Nightlife Society | VIP Club Nights"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/4/9/6/c/highres_522678796.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/7/6/d/highres_527105997.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/7/2/8/6/highres_535829318.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/9/1/2/3/highres_536377155.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/d/d/c/6/highres_535916774.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/8/1/3/5/highres_535713077.jpeg" as="image" data-nex